Real problem: Billions in public contracts are awarded to politically connected vendors — but the data exists in fragmented, dirty formats nobody has cleaned.
Ingest USAspending.gov contract awards. Clean and normalize vendor names (same company appears 50 ways). 
Flag statistical anomalies: single-bid contracts, contracts awarded just below approval thresholds, same vendor winning repeatedly in one agency.
Build a scoring model for "contracts worth investigating."

